# Personal notes in docs/ — OKRs, performance-review evidence, employer business
# context, reading lists. These stay on disk but out of the repo: they name real
# colleagues, comp figures and internal funnel data that do not belong in a
# codebase that may be shared or made public.
#
# Default-deny by design, so a new personal note is never committed by accident.
# To track a doc that is genuinely about THIS codebase, add a `!docs/<name>.md`
# line below.
#
# Pattern is `docs/*.md`, not `docs/` — git cannot re-include a file whose parent
# directory is excluded, so the negations below would silently do nothing.
docs/*.md
!docs/amplitude-integration.md
!docs/api-usage-audit-2026-10-13.md
!docs/diploma-collaboration-strategy.md
!docs/feature-plan-calendar-ux-and-landing.md
!docs/feature-plan-telegram-notifications-mobile.md
